        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0217" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/4–352: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, Far East (Ridgway) to the
                        Joint Chiefs of Staff</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>operational immediate</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-04-29T18:04:00+09:00">April 29, 1952—6:04
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>CX 67738. Re C 67178.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d108-f1"/> Available data on Opn <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Scatter</hi> as of 28 Apr is shown below: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Total number screened to return to Communist control: NK POWs 25492,
                            SK POWs 4240, CCF 5202, CIs 3657, total 38591.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The total number of unscreened POWs and CIs in compounds where
                            screening has not been initiated: NK POWs 39471, SK POWs 263, CCF 1147,
                            CIs 6449, total 47330.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Results to date of rescreening those who initially were screened and
                            elected to remain in the UNC custody: <list>
                                <item>Col A. Initially screened to remain with UNC; NK 31369, SK
                                    11602, CCF 14487, CI 26120, total 83578.</item>
                                <item>Col B. Number of those Col A rescreened; NK 29179, SK 10987,
                                    CCF 14127, CI 21059, total 75352.</item>
                                <item>Col C. Total number remaining in UNC custody after
                                    rescreening; NK 29062, SK 10906, CCF 13712, CI 20919, total
                                    74599.</item>
                                <item>Col D. Total number who reversed decision and are to return to
                                    Communists; NK 117, SK 81, CCF 415, CI 140, total 753.</item>
                            </list></item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Shipment from Koje-Do of those who will be retained in UNC custody
                            after rescreening: NK POWs 19045, SK POWs 9043, CCF 10712, CIs 15974,
                            total 54774.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
        </body>
